#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059642 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059470 :question/id #uuid "f2b7e482-2bcd-5bd2-91ee-66415b375da4" :question/math-academy-id "e-3137" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta}{\\sin\\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta}\t=\t\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\cdot (\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta)} {\\sin \\theta}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (1)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta} = \\cot \\theta.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049181 :topic/math-academy-id 423 :topic/title "Simplifying Rational Expressions by Factoring"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060345 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907031aa-def2-5346-b05d-e1bb6356bb7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\tan θ - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058693} {:answer/id #uuid "a08fa882-3190-566d-b2f4-0ed8fd4b937a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\tan θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058694} {:answer/id #uuid "a0aee8d5-2045-56ab-bd31-028c9587b3f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\tan θ" :db/id #edb/ref 175921860586